# Doors, switches and trip-wires (§3.2.2).
#
# Shaped like a converted Doom map rather than like a hand-authored one,
# because the thing under test is the path a converted map takes: a door is a
# SECTOR whose ceiling rests on its floor, opened by working the side in front
# of it; a trip-wire is a side marked `trigger`, crossed rather than pushed.
#
#   room A  --[door]--  room B1  |  room B2  --[lift]
#            side 2               trip-wire
#
# The east wing's ceiling is 1.5 -- a Doom 72-unit doorway -- so the door opens
# to 1.4167 (its lowest neighbouring ceiling less Doom's four units) and the
# body has to FIT through it. The engine's default 2.0 body does not, which is
# the whole reason a map states the proportions it was built for.
#
# The door is shut in the geometry (ceil == floor), exactly as Doom stores one,
# so "the door opened" is a claim about the ceiling having moved and not about
# a flag somewhere.

sector floor 0 ceil 8 tag 1 light 200 floortex FLOOR4_8 ceiltex CEIL3_5
  vertex 0 0    wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 10 0   wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 10 3   neighbor 1
  vertex 10 7   wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 10 10  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 0 10   wall tex STARTAN3
end

# The door. Closed: its ceiling sits on its floor.
sector floor 0 ceil 0 tag 2 light 160 floortex FLOOR4_8 ceiltex CEIL3_5
  vertex 10 3  wall tex DOORSTOP
  vertex 12 3  neighbor 2
  vertex 12 7  wall tex DOORSTOP
  vertex 10 7  neighbor 0
end

sector floor 0 ceil 1.5 tag 3 light 200 floortex FLOOR4_8 ceiltex CEIL3_5
  vertex 12 0   wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 17 0   neighbor 3 trigger
  vertex 17 10  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 12 10  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 12 7   neighbor 1
  vertex 12 3   wall tex STARTAN3
end

sector floor 0 ceil 1.5 tag 4 light 200 floortex FLOOR4_8 ceiltex CEIL3_5
  vertex 17 0   wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 22 0   wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 22 3   neighbor 4
  vertex 22 7   wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 22 10  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 17 10  neighbor 2 trigger
end

# The lift, parked up at 3 so lowering it to its lowest neighbour is visible.
sector floor 3 ceil 8 tag 5 light 180 floortex FLOOR4_8 ceiltex CEIL3_5
  vertex 22 3  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 26 3  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 26 7  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 22 7  neighbor 3
end

# Doom's player at 1/48: a 16-unit radius and a 56-unit height. Stated here
# because the door's opening is 1.5 tall -- a Doom 72-unit doorway -- and the
# engine's default 2.0 body does not fit through it.
body radius 0.3333 height 1.1667

# What this map needs to behave. mapc copies both next to the baked map, and
# the server loads them from there -- no --script arguments required.
script scripts/doom.lua
script doors_lines.lua

spawn start 5 5 1
spawn behind_door 14 5 1
